  "id": "acoustic",
  "term": "acoustic",
  "definition": "In this speech-assessment context, acoustic refers to the measurable sound properties of speech, such as vowel frequencies, duration, and variability. These sound-based measures can help describe speech patterns in some autistic subgroups, but they are not established as a single universal marker across autism.",
